    "body": "Adds an `explore ... in` keyword that invokes a new stepper, like `theorem`, but for non-booleans. The explore body itself doesn't evaluate to anything. However, unknown variables are assumed to be \"free\" and of their assumed type in the stepper, suppressing warnings and supporting algebraic variables. \r\n\r\n<img width=\"696\" height=\"377\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-19 at 1 21 28\u202fAM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/69b2fb24-57df-4683-bccd-7caf4cf1c51d\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n<img width=\"378\" height=\"267\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-01 at 6 17 46\u202fPM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/56ecc27e-7000-44a5-b01b-7e700b530212\" />",
